  "explanation_rules_vs_learned": "Tuned Rules achieves Test F1 = 0.8389 vs. Logistic Regression Test F1 = 0.9207. In clean synthetic benchmark environments (SciFig-Controlled v2), lexical overlap features (exact substring containment and trigram Jaccard) provide virtually deterministic binary indicators of ground truth links without noise. Tuned rules apply a discrete threshold directly to this pure lexical signal without estimating continuous coefficients. In contrast, Logistic Regression optimizes continuous weights across 10 correlated pairwise features subject to L2 regularization shrinkage, which can introduce slight decision threshold miscalibration between the validation tuning set and held-out test figures.",
